        "original_id": "0e89b86f-08a7-5456-891f-bfda733aea2b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Animals: Pseudaelurus, Pantherinae, Proailurus\n- People: Reginald Innes Pocock\n- Concepts: Felidae, felines, machairodont saber-tooths\n\nFacts:\n- Pseudaelurus succeeded Proailurus.\n- Pseudaelurus is an ancestor of modern felines, Pantherinae, and the extinct machairodont saber-tooths.\n- In 1917, Reginald Innes Pocock named and first described Pantherinae.\n- Pantherinae is a subfamily within the cat family Felidae.",
